From 008c7b2386fd924ede210c9dda3b68e622d66c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:05:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] feat(motion): multi-axis deburr kernel - tilted cone
 flank on the chamfer plane, holder tilt-away

Share the 3D Deburr's exposed-edge scan (deburr_scan) and pose a
tilted cone per edge stretch: Axis5 leans about the chamfer normal
inside max tilt, Axis4 keeps the rotary plane; the shank test picks
the clear pose nearest the last one, or the edge follows the
unreachable-edge policy.

Refs #1894

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
