From 800d05c571a5ddc2faef588ef1d3c1921852d43a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:21:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] feat(multiaxis): Multi-Axis Deburr operation - kind 46,
 project arm, generate arm, page, MCP

Append OpType::MultiAxisDeburr (ordinal 46, Section::MultiAxis) with
the Deburr fields plus axis_mode, lead_deg, lag_deg, max_tilt_deg and
shank_avoid. The kernel enters and leaves along the tool axis, turns
the axis in the air, and ends a run at a chamfer-plane corner, so the
verify and post laws pass on a tilt-head machine.

Refs #1894

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
